# Cross-harness continuation

When resuming existing repository work, use `cross-harness-handoff` to check shared ECC project memory before asking the user to repeat context. Verify recalled state against current Git/source/spec/ADR; the repository is authoritative. Pass its absolute Git root as `workspaceRoot` to ECC MCP calls. For a harness/session transfer, save a concise durable handoff through that skill. Details stay on-demand at `~/.agents/skills/cross-harness-handoff/SKILL.md`.

# Browser verification

Prefer the existing functional native browser/computer-use capability for relevant interactive browser tasks. Use `agent-browser` only as an on-demand fallback or when explicitly requested. Use uniquely named isolated sessions and close your own session afterward. Scope checks to browser implications; backend-only, browser-unrelated C++/C#, documentation-only, unrelated Git, and trivial non-browser changes need no browser launch. Choose one frontend owner: `impeccable` normally, `redesign-existing-projects` for requested whole-app redesign; differentiated image/style requests use their specialist. User/project brand and supplied references win.
